<Base title="Privacy, browser-local progress and data controls"><article class="container"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR WORKING NOTES</span><h1>Your plan stays<br/>in your browser.</h1><p class="lede">This release does not accept account registrations, uploads, payments or server-stored expansion plans.</p></div><div class="article-body" style="max-width:800px"><h2>Planning information</h2><p>Tools calculate in your browser. Saving a draft on this device is optional. If enabled, local storage retains the working plan in the browser profile you are using. Other people using that same browser profile may access it. Avoid confidential customer names, personal records, bank details and sensitive contracts.</p><p>Use the reset control in the planning workspace to remove the saved draft, or clear this site’s storage in your browser settings. JSON export and the printable brief are created locally; you choose where to save or share them. Clearing site data may permanently remove an unexported draft.</p><h2>No tracking integration</h2><p>This build has no advertising pixels, analytics service, third-party chat widget or cookie-based account system. Fonts and application assets are served with the site. Ordinary external source links take you to the named publisher, which has its own privacy terms.</p><h2>Hosting requests and logs</h2><p>The hosting provider processes ordinary HTTP request information, which can include IP address, request path, browser information and timestamps. The application does not log plan inputs or transmit them to the server. Plan values are not included in URLs, indexing surfaces or shared page caches.</p><p>Hosting-provider retention, international transfers and access arrangements must be confirmed by the site operator for the actual deployment. This notice should be updated if analytics, contact forms, accounts or document storage are introduced.</p><h2>Operational details still to supply</h2><p>The project owner has not yet supplied a public controller identity, privacy contact, retention policy for hosting logs, or confirmed hosting arrangements. These are recorded release tasks. The site does not advertise a service or collect leads while those details remain open.</p><p>For European and Southeast Asian audiences, the operator must assess the applicable privacy rules and any consent requirements against actual processing and establishment. This version avoids optional tracking; it does not claim that this alone resolves every privacy obligation.</p><h2>What a reset cannot remove</h2><p>A reset removes this application’s browser-local draft. It cannot delete copies you exported, browser backups, shared files or routine provider access logs. There is no server-side plan record to retrieve or share with another user.</p></div></article></Base>
